  "number": 415,
  "html_url": "https://github.com/just-every/run-lamp/pull/415",
  "title": "Import Sorry notice and update templates into private composers",
  "body": "Sorry notice and update templates now move into private composers with complete wording, optional subject, collection-page scope and source timestamps. Capture validates every documented page; missing pages, conflicting wording variants and foreign scope refuse the input. Applying wording preserves operator choices, and oversized wording can be shortened while the original remains available.\n\nBoth kinds support repeat protection and conflict-preserving undo. The additive 0083 migration preserves existing templates. No clause status judgments are changed.\n\nValidation: ordered source/build checks, 27 templates of each kind over 25-row pages, exact metadata/body API reads, eight refusal cases, repeat and named conditional undo, and composer/Settings proof at 1440 and 390. Generated contract views are retained from main for the lander to regenerate under the seed contract.\n\nExact-SHA Verify [44192808371](https://github.com/just-every/run-lamp/actions/runs/44192808371) completed on `8b94d56ba4cd6a2e727a182adac6af6f19b147e3`. Its only root failure is the expected `ACCEPTANCE.md` generator check; artifact/aggregate failures and skipped shards follow from that step. This is the seed contract\u2019s explicit generated-view exception. Local ordered build steps and touched public-door proofs passed; the lander regenerates the views before its independent gate.\n",
